WEBVTT

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:09.625
"F City Big Sight Comics Market"

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:17.125
<i>Dojin-Dojin-Dojinshi!</i>
We'd die if we didn't buy comic books!

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:22.917
"Rikdokan"   "New Title"
"Come on over!!"  "In Stock"  "Koshi Rikdo"

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:27.542
"Warning: This scene is fictional.
It's not selling.

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:29.000
"Warning: This scene is fictional.
I knew it.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.417
It really does sell, no kidding..."
Sure, it became an anime,

00:00:30.417 --> 00:00:31.833
It really does sell, no kidding..."
but it's a quack experiment.

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.083
It really does sell, no kidding..."
There's no way the original books

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:34.833
It really does sell, no kidding..."
would sell with the same luck.

00:00:34.833 --> 00:00:38.417
I guess it can't be helped.
It's not my fault, after all.

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:41.292
Excuse me, about your
earlier publications...

00:00:41.292 --> 00:00:46.167
Oh, I'm sorry. The older stuff
isn't scheduled to be reprinted...

00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:52.833
What?!

00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:55.625
Mr. Rikdo, the cat's out of the bag.

00:00:55.625 --> 00:00:57.500
We know you used to write a comic

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.292
that became the prototype for Excel Saga.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:01.667
Uh-oh!

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:04.917
We've just about run out of
material from the original work.

00:01:04.917 --> 00:01:06.958
Please give us your permission.

00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:08.167
Uh-oh! No!

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:12.417
I don't want to be at
the mercy of my old stories!

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.833
Quit strugglin' Riku-<i>chan</i>, man.

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:17.917
D-D-D-Director, you too?!

00:01:17.917 --> 00:01:20.708
A-A-And somehow my seal too?!

00:01:20.708 --> 00:01:22.208
Do it!

00:01:22.208 --> 00:01:23.875
With pleasure!

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:28.542
No!

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:46.500
<i>Sore wa ai ja nai</i>

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.375
<i>Ai wa sore ja nai</i>

00:01:50.375 --> 00:01:58.292
<i>Aishite iru kedo aisarete wa inai</i>

00:01:58.292 --> 00:02:02.208
<i>Kesshite ai ja nai</i>

00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:06.250
<i>Ketsu wa ai ja nai</i>

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:13.958
<i>Aisaretai keredo motometari wa shinai</i>

00:02:14.792 --> 00:02:18.667
<i>Kono mi sasagete inochi nagedashi</i>

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:22.750
<i>Wakime mo furazu tada hitasura ni</i>

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.625
<i>Damashite sukashite yokohairi</i>

00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:29.875
<i>Tanin o fumitaoshi keri o kamashite</i>

00:02:29.875 --> 00:02:32.042
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:33.958
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:35.833
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>
<i>(Tonzura koite!)</i>

00:02:35.833 --> 00:02:37.792
<i>Tonzura koite!</i>

00:02:37.792 --> 00:02:42.625
<i>Banana no kawa de korondemo</i>

00:02:42.625 --> 00:02:45.750
<i>Sore wa subete ano kata no tame</i>

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:50.333
<i>Shiite iu nara sore wa kitto</i>

00:02:50.333 --> 00:02:58.167
<i>Ai to iu na no chuuseishin</i>

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.833
Mr. Watanabe!

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.667
Wait for me, Miss Ayasugi!

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.417
Wait for me!

00:03:31.208 --> 00:03:33.292
I've got you now.

00:03:33.292 --> 00:03:35.042
Mr. Watanabe...

00:03:40.333 --> 00:03:41.750
<i>I know.</i>

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:45.542
<i>This is a dream. I know it well.</i>

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:47.583
<i>That show I saw yesterday</i>
<i>that had a fictional person</i>

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>involved in the French Revolution.</i>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.833
<i>Or the one where a girl out</i>
<i>on a journey in search of a flower</i>

00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:54.333
<i>that's at her home all along</i>
<i>while being pursued by a stalker.</i>

00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.000
<i>Those anime reruns</i>
<i>must be the cause of this.</i>

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.375
<i>Really, I'm appalled</i>
<i>at my lack of imagination.</i>

00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:01.208
<i>But still... But...</i>

00:04:01.208 --> 00:04:02.958
Mr. Watanabe?

00:04:04.125 --> 00:04:05.625
--But bear with me, just for now!

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:06.375
--That hurts! Don't squeeze so hard! Gross!
--But bear with me, just for now!

00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:09.125
--That hurts! Don't squeeze so hard! Gross!
--I'm a man who can only be honest with himself in his dreams!

00:04:09.125 --> 00:04:14.333
Mr. Watanabe, I can no longer wait.

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:16.000
M-Miss Ayasugi...

00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:21.417
Miss Ayasugi?!

00:04:21.417 --> 00:04:26.042
What is this?
What happened? This stuff...

00:04:27.042 --> 00:04:30.875
No matter what the environment, I... I...

00:04:41.542 --> 00:04:45.958
What a typical punch line.
I fell, but it didn't fall.

00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:48.250
There's a limit
to how quack you can get.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:49.583
Damn it!

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.000
But why am I having
such a hard time breathing?

00:04:56.542 --> 00:04:57.542
What the heck?

00:04:57.542 --> 00:05:01.250
I don't remember watching
any live action hero show reruns.

00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:04.250
Oh, it's that.

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:07.792
What was it? The line
you say at a time like this is...

00:05:08.792 --> 00:05:10.125
What the hell is this?!

00:05:10.708 --> 00:05:13.292
Hello, we are reporting to you
live from in front of

00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:16.042
the City Emergency Countermeasure
Headquarters Building.

00:05:16.042 --> 00:05:18.875
Right now, the crime in this
city goes practically unchecked.

00:05:18.875 --> 00:05:20.958
What kind of brake can be applied?

00:05:20.958 --> 00:05:24.125
Currently, a system to
deal with this immediately...

00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:25.125
Gentlemen,

00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:27.792
this city is being exposed
to an unprecedented danger!

00:05:27.792 --> 00:05:30.042
Numerous incidents of illegal
parking of cars and bicycles,

00:05:30.042 --> 00:05:31.750
ignoring traffic lights,
and exceeding the speed limit!

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.333
Tardy people, spoiled children, and liars.

00:05:33.333 --> 00:05:35.792
Immoral authors. Directors that
tend to not take responsibility.

00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:38.208
Script writers who don't consider
the trouble they cause others.

00:05:38.208 --> 00:05:40.917
The city is overflowing with
all of these crimes!

00:05:40.917 --> 00:05:42.542
This is truly a city crisis!

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:43.792
--It's an emergency situation!

00:05:43.792 --> 00:05:44.792
--Let's deal with it!
--It's an emergency situation!

00:05:44.792 --> 00:05:46.292
But how?

00:05:46.292 --> 00:05:49.375
Please leave that matter to me.

00:05:49.375 --> 00:05:50.833
Y-You are...

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:51.792
Kabapu!

00:05:51.792 --> 00:05:53.125
Mr. Kabapu!

00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:54.083
Kaba!

00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:55.083
Kaba-kaba!

00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:55.500
--Kaba!

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.375
Mr. Kabapu, I acknowledge your abilities
but I cannot believe

00:05:59.375 --> 00:06:03.125
that you can save the city
from this crisis by yourself!

00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:04.750
I cannot believe it either.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.125
--I would like you to believe it.

00:06:06.125 --> 00:06:07.333
--How?!
--I would like you to believe it.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:09.500
This is what I have gathered them for!

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.167
Six shadowy agents
operating in the public light!

00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:18.750
All of it is to protect
this beautiful city!

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.667
Hail, Ilpalazzo!

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:22.333
"by Excel"

00:06:22.542 --> 00:06:25.125
Oh, I went reverse from
America and when I realized,

00:06:25.125 --> 00:06:27.458
I was in New Zealand
and I panicked like crazy.

00:06:27.458 --> 00:06:29.833
But I skinned the organisms
that were all over the place,

00:06:29.833 --> 00:06:31.333
put them towards my travel expenses,

00:06:31.333 --> 00:06:32.875
and somehow made my way back!

00:06:32.875 --> 00:06:34.667
Then I find that it's a
special holiday at ACROSS,

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:35.875
so what a surprise that was!

00:06:35.875 --> 00:06:38.583
But as the Excel that
serves Lord Ilpalazzo devotedly,

00:06:38.583 --> 00:06:41.625
I felt that I absolutely
must report my return,

00:06:41.625 --> 00:06:43.875
and so I am simulating giving my report.

00:06:43.875 --> 00:06:46.542
Please don't ask why
we're doing it in a place like this.

00:06:46.542 --> 00:06:47.917
That is all! End report!

00:06:47.917 --> 00:06:50.333
Welcome home, Senior Excel.

00:06:50.333 --> 00:06:52.667
I wish you'd say things like
that when I actually came back,

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:53.875
but that's okay.

00:06:53.875 --> 00:06:56.250
More importantly, Hatchan,
why don't we independently

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:58.042
go out to conquer the city today?

00:06:58.042 --> 00:07:02.208
If we suddenly conquered it,
Lord Ilpalazzo is sure to be surprised!

00:07:02.208 --> 00:07:03.875
That was a predictable pun, wasn't it?

00:07:03.875 --> 00:07:07.875
"Ilpalazzo City"

00:07:08.583 --> 00:07:10.875
Excel, I am absolutely surprised

00:07:10.875 --> 00:07:13.875
that you've suddenly accomplished
the conquest of this city.

00:07:13.875 --> 00:07:17.042
Please praise me!
Please take me, Lord Ilpalazzo!

00:07:18.375 --> 00:07:20.125
Come, Excel.

00:07:20.125 --> 00:07:22.917
Why, of course,
I'm coming super-right away!

00:07:22.917 --> 00:07:24.458
Defense! Defense!

00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:26.333
Offense! Offense!

00:07:26.333 --> 00:07:26.750
--Defense... Offense...

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.625
--Senior? Senior, it's over.
--Defense... Offense...

00:07:29.625 --> 00:07:31.958
Well, it was wishful,
but that's what it'll be like.

00:07:31.958 --> 00:07:34.042
So, let's conquer!
Go, go, conquer!

00:07:34.042 --> 00:07:36.000
Our present goal is to
make the ignorant masses suffer

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.417
and make it so they don't have
to worry about tomorrow's dinner!

00:07:38.417 --> 00:07:39.917
Yay! We did it! Splendid!

00:07:39.917 --> 00:07:42.583
And what, specifically, shall we do?

00:07:45.875 --> 00:07:47.750
"A journey of a thousand
leagues starts with a single step."

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.583
In other words,
we'll start with the details

00:07:49.583 --> 00:07:51.583
and go for building
a mountain out of molehills!

00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:53.042
Having returned from America,

00:07:53.042 --> 00:07:55.417
it seems that your
vocabulary has increased.

00:07:55.417 --> 00:07:57.750
Okay, of course, of course.

00:08:00.083 --> 00:08:03.500
What the hell is this?
I want to deny this design too!

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:05.583
I-It won't come off! I can't undress!

00:08:05.583 --> 00:08:06.875
There's no seams or zippers!

00:08:06.875 --> 00:08:08.292
Damn, what the hell is up with this?

00:08:08.292 --> 00:08:12.000
Are they gonna do a masked
youth legend in the 21st century?!

00:08:15.833 --> 00:08:18.833
Man, you're noisy!
What are you making a fuss about?!

00:08:18.833 --> 00:08:21.167
That voice! Iwata!

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.167
You guys too?!

00:08:23.167 --> 00:08:24.583
Don't I look cool?

00:08:24.583 --> 00:08:28.125
How can you accept this
abnormal situation so calmly?!

00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:30.458
You're the one who should accept reality!

00:08:30.458 --> 00:08:31.958
You could panic a little!

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:34.458
That possibility is greater than 100%.

00:08:34.458 --> 00:08:36.667
What I want to know is
not about how we're dressed,

00:08:36.667 --> 00:08:39.083
but <i>who </i>dressed me in this thing.

00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:40.125
--Me! Me!
--but <i>who </i>dressed me in this thing.

00:08:40.125 --> 00:08:44.583
Mr. Kabapu asked me,
so I changed your clothes, Sister Misaki!

00:08:44.583 --> 00:08:48.333
Why you! Even I haven't
seen Misaki's body yet...

00:08:48.333 --> 00:08:49.292
Or rather, tell me!

00:08:49.292 --> 00:08:51.875
Characters like her always
have a mole somewhere!

00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:53.875
Tell me! Spill it! Talk!

00:08:55.875 --> 00:08:58.833
And the obligatory twinkle!

00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:02.583
Sister, you're awesome!
That monkey just went flying!

00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:06.042
In other words,
that's the power of these suits.

00:09:06.042 --> 00:09:08.208
No matter how I analyze
the material of the costumes,

00:09:08.208 --> 00:09:12.333
it is only composed of FRP,
nylon fiber, and vinyl chloride.

00:09:13.458 --> 00:09:15.667
Hello, my friends.

00:09:15.667 --> 00:09:16.667
Mr. Kabapu!

00:09:16.667 --> 00:09:20.083
How do those Daiten Suits fit?

00:09:20.083 --> 00:09:23.500
So it was you that
came up with this sick plan!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.833
Be very wary of catching colds.

00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:28.417
Never mind that! Tell us
how to take these outfits off!

00:09:28.417 --> 00:09:29.500
Right now!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.958
Only the man who developed
those Daiten Suits, Shioji,

00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:33.708
knows how to remove them.

00:09:33.708 --> 00:09:36.125
On top of that, he is not here,
due to some circumstances.

00:09:36.125 --> 00:09:38.083
What kind of circumstances?!

00:09:38.083 --> 00:09:39.542
It's probably the budget.

00:09:39.542 --> 00:09:40.750
Shut up!

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.583
Calm down.

00:09:43.375 --> 00:09:45.792
I'll make one thing clear for you.

00:09:45.792 --> 00:09:48.292
You guys are members of
the Department of City Security.

00:09:48.292 --> 00:09:49.083
In other words,

00:09:49.083 --> 00:09:52.042
you are envoys of justice
that protect the peace in this city.

00:09:52.042 --> 00:09:54.375
And that's why you're telling us
to wear these and work?!

00:09:54.375 --> 00:09:55.875
Do you not care for the idea?

00:09:55.875 --> 00:09:56.750
Of course not!

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.125
Oh, Sister Misaki!

00:09:59.125 --> 00:10:02.333
Getting a six-month pay cut
for ignoring your superior's orders

00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:05.125
and receiving a bonus when
you accomplish this special mission

00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:07.375
comes down to a difference
in excess of six digits.

00:10:07.375 --> 00:10:08.583
Everyone decided?!

00:10:08.583 --> 00:10:10.333
"Yeah"
Yeah!

00:10:10.333 --> 00:10:13.875
Very well. And now,
I will tell you your codenames!

00:10:14.708 --> 00:10:16.417
Daiten Ism!

00:10:16.417 --> 00:10:17.917
Me?!

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:19.250
Daiten Aigan!

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.500
"You gonna eat?"   "Curry..."

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:23.375
Daiten Ladies!

00:10:23.375 --> 00:10:25.083
My head hurts.

00:10:25.083 --> 00:10:26.917
Daiten Core!

00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:28.250
Are you alive?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:32.042
And you two are
Daiten Solaria One and Two!

00:10:32.042 --> 00:10:35.583
The peace of this city
rests on your shoulders!

00:10:35.583 --> 00:10:37.708
I will christen you now!

00:10:37.708 --> 00:10:42.000
The six of you together
are the Daitenzin!

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.000
The Municipal Force Daitenzin!

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:48.875
"Municipal Force Daitenzin"

00:11:06.292 --> 00:11:08.167
Hurry up and get fighting!

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:09.833
S-Sorry.

00:11:10.792 --> 00:11:13.458
Prepare yourself, Gomez!

00:11:13.458 --> 00:11:14.417
Mr. Pe!

00:11:14.417 --> 00:11:15.792
Dear!

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:20.708
Unforgivable Gomez!
Annoying Gomez!

00:11:20.708 --> 00:11:23.292
I've sweated and even shed a few tears,

00:11:23.292 --> 00:11:26.667
playing out my part in
this incredibly wretched story!

00:11:26.667 --> 00:11:28.708
But, but, but!

00:11:28.708 --> 00:11:31.042
I will turn the tables as of today!

00:11:31.042 --> 00:11:33.958
I will defeat you and then go
back to being the peaceful Mr. Pe!

00:11:33.958 --> 00:11:37.542
Take this! Pedro Punch of Anger!

00:11:37.542 --> 00:11:39.042
Have you eaten?!

00:11:39.042 --> 00:11:40.833
Brush your teeth!

00:11:40.833 --> 00:11:42.667
See you next week!

00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:45.708
Fool.

00:11:46.542 --> 00:11:48.000
One more time, Mr. Pe!

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:50.917
One more time, Dear!

00:11:50.917 --> 00:11:52.875
Wh-Why?

00:11:52.875 --> 00:11:54.792
I am a ghost.

00:11:54.792 --> 00:11:58.000
In other words, why can you
hit me when I'm a spiritual being?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:12:01.250
Don't you realize, Pedro?
There is a reason.

00:12:10.792 --> 00:12:12.458
N-No...

00:12:12.458 --> 00:12:13.958
You are...

00:12:17.417 --> 00:12:18.958
That Man!

00:12:18.958 --> 00:12:20.833
If I couldn't at least
do something like this,

00:12:20.833 --> 00:12:24.708
I wouldn't be the Great Will of
the Macrocosm's "That Man", fool.

00:12:24.708 --> 00:12:26.792
Wh-Why?

00:12:26.792 --> 00:12:29.375
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:29.375 --> 00:12:32.708
I-It's pointless to notice it so late,

00:12:32.708 --> 00:12:36.792
but th-the two of you have the same voice.

00:12:36.792 --> 00:12:38.958
You're exactly right.

00:12:38.958 --> 00:12:41.958
So you finally noticed, you fool!

00:12:43.792 --> 00:12:46.792
Shoot, I'm too late!

00:12:46.792 --> 00:12:48.375
--No!

00:12:48.375 --> 00:12:50.375
--I really <i>was </i>too late!
--No!

00:13:03.875 --> 00:13:06.417
People are paying a lot of attention to us.

00:13:06.417 --> 00:13:07.917
"In more ways than one..."

00:13:08.083 --> 00:13:10.208
This is practically like the
Emperor's New Clothes.

00:13:10.208 --> 00:13:12.542
But at least we know it.

00:13:12.542 --> 00:13:15.333
Now, what should we do?

00:13:15.333 --> 00:13:16.792
"Take these clothes... Off!!"

00:13:17.292 --> 00:13:20.417
What?! We're gonna take them off?!
But they look so cool!

00:13:20.417 --> 00:13:22.167
You've got to be kidding me.

00:13:22.167 --> 00:13:24.833
You have been given one
mission and one mission only!

00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:26.417
Do not let evil get away!

00:13:26.417 --> 00:13:28.583
That's right, you must not
overlook any evil in this city,

00:13:28.583 --> 00:13:29.875
no matter how insignificant it is!

00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:32.542
I'd like you to resolve at
least ten incidents.

00:13:33.417 --> 00:13:34.667
But you know...

00:13:34.667 --> 00:13:37.458
Maybe it's a sham, but public
peace is thorough in this country.

00:13:37.458 --> 00:13:39.833
I don't think such incidents
will just pop up like that.

00:13:39.833 --> 00:13:41.625
They can be insignificant!

00:13:41.625 --> 00:13:42.625
And then...

00:13:42.625 --> 00:13:43.833
"We'll be free."

00:13:45.333 --> 00:13:46.833
Littering!

00:13:47.792 --> 00:13:48.667
"Justice"

00:13:48.958 --> 00:13:50.208
Leave it to me!

00:13:50.208 --> 00:13:52.042
Best Electron!

00:13:57.792 --> 00:13:58.917
Overkill.

00:13:58.917 --> 00:14:00.625
Wha-What the...

00:14:00.625 --> 00:14:03.000
I just shouted whatever
and these gun things came out!

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.000
Is this a power of the suits too?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:06.958
We're better off not worrying
about this any further.

00:14:06.958 --> 00:14:07.958
"It's obligatory."

00:14:07.958 --> 00:14:10.917
But with this, the city has become
that much more peaceful.

00:14:10.917 --> 00:14:13.292
I'm not really happy
with this, but I understand.

00:14:13.292 --> 00:14:15.792
Let's just keep it up
at the pace we're going!

00:14:16.583 --> 00:14:17.125
All right!

00:14:17.125 --> 00:14:19.375
"Municipal Force Daitenzin"

00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:22.292
Lend me some change, like 200 yen.

00:14:22.292 --> 00:14:24.333
Pay me back tomorrow, okay?

00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:26.083
That's extortion.

00:14:26.083 --> 00:14:29.333
Wha-What are you talking about,
you crazy bastard?!

00:14:29.333 --> 00:14:30.833
We're brothers.

00:14:30.833 --> 00:14:32.667
Giga Smash!

00:14:34.417 --> 00:14:35.125
--We won! We won! We're winning all the time!

00:14:35.125 --> 00:14:36.750
--B-Bro, 200 yen...
--We won! We won! We're winning all the time!

00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:37.833
--We beat them! We beat them!

00:14:37.833 --> 00:14:39.833
--Thank you.
--We pushed them over!

00:14:39.833 --> 00:14:42.833
That was extortion, right?

00:14:42.833 --> 00:14:44.333
You lose if you think about it.

00:14:44.333 --> 00:14:46.500
"Municipal Force Daitenzin"

00:14:46.875 --> 00:14:48.542
Satoshi, you idiot!

00:14:48.542 --> 00:14:51.750
Aw, come on, Akari!
Can't I even kiss you?

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:53.958
But I'm still...

00:14:53.958 --> 00:14:55.625
Delta End!

00:14:55.625 --> 00:14:57.833
We haven't done anything yet!

00:14:57.875 --> 00:15:00.083
"Municipal Force Daitenzin"

00:15:00.625 --> 00:15:03.042
Chief, when will you and your wife...

00:15:03.042 --> 00:15:06.583
Wait for me. We're having
problems about our children.

00:15:06.583 --> 00:15:08.833
The baby inside me is your--

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:10.542
"Scot Bomber!"

00:15:12.542 --> 00:15:14.542
That one looked like justice.

00:15:15.708 --> 00:15:16.792
"The Daitenzin Go!"

00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:18.875
Tenzin Dynamic!

00:15:18.875 --> 00:15:20.000
"The Daitenzin Go More!"

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:20.500
--Catharsis Wave!

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.125
--Train station!
--Catharsis Wave!

00:15:22.125 --> 00:15:23.208
"The Daitenzin Go Even Further!"

00:15:23.208 --> 00:15:23.875
"Galactic Illusion!"

00:15:23.875 --> 00:15:25.208
Tower!

00:15:25.208 --> 00:15:26.167
"They Go Persistently!"

00:15:26.708 --> 00:15:27.500
--Vega Spectron!

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:29.292
--Here it comes!
--Vega Spectron!

00:15:36.125 --> 00:15:37.792
That was the eighth one.

00:15:37.792 --> 00:15:38.875
Two more to go.

00:15:38.875 --> 00:15:41.208
We're going after even
the really insignificant stuff,

00:15:41.208 --> 00:15:43.875
but there still
aren't that many incidents.

00:15:43.875 --> 00:15:47.667
Damn it, the people in this
city are too wastefully moral!

00:15:47.667 --> 00:15:48.833
Look!

00:15:48.833 --> 00:15:50.750
They're crossing at the crosswalk
with their hands up.

00:15:50.750 --> 00:15:53.083
I'm beginning to hate
that old woman in green.

00:15:53.083 --> 00:15:55.792
Fine, we'll have to split up and
search for evil deeds.

00:15:55.792 --> 00:15:58.417
Starting now, spitting on the
road will be a felony!

00:15:58.417 --> 00:16:00.542
This is all for the sake of our freedom!

00:16:00.542 --> 00:16:01.417
Roger!

00:16:01.417 --> 00:16:03.542
So, we three

00:16:03.542 --> 00:16:06.042
will go search in that direction,
nice and friendly like.

00:16:06.042 --> 00:16:07.750
You guys skulk
about there and stay alive,

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.333
or you could go die too.

00:16:10.333 --> 00:16:12.000
Double Gigalot!

00:16:15.417 --> 00:16:17.375
"Living is a hard thing to do."

00:16:17.375 --> 00:16:19.542
You don't have to think
about it. Don't think about it.

00:16:19.542 --> 00:16:20.625
Now, let's go.

00:16:20.625 --> 00:16:23.417
Okay, Sister!

00:16:23.417 --> 00:16:24.417
M-Me too...

00:16:24.417 --> 00:16:26.917
Just barely stay alive,
or else make sure to stay dead.

00:16:26.917 --> 00:16:29.542
Fingers know everything.

00:16:29.542 --> 00:16:33.125
They know too
much about deep inside!

00:16:33.125 --> 00:16:34.833
Did we get something, Senior?

00:16:34.833 --> 00:16:37.875
This feel! This warmth!
Definitely not an arcade coin!

00:16:37.875 --> 00:16:39.125
Definitely not a counterfeit!

00:16:39.125 --> 00:16:42.292
Truly an item of value, a product
of Japan's minting technology!

00:16:42.292 --> 00:16:45.542
All right! Got ten yen! Yay, yay, yay!

00:16:45.542 --> 00:16:47.417
We've done it, Senior.

00:16:47.417 --> 00:16:50.833
Surely, this is the result
of your nightly finger training.

00:16:50.833 --> 00:16:51.500
--Oh, please, Hatchan, it's embarrassing!

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.125
--Oh, there... my... heart...
--Oh, please, Hatchan, it's embarrassing!

00:16:53.125 --> 00:16:55.125
--Oh, there... my... heart...
--That wasn't training!

00:16:55.125 --> 00:16:57.625
Well, that aside, 230 yen from
going around to sixty places.

00:16:57.625 --> 00:16:59.833
Surpass a 30% hit rate,
and I can own the position of lead hitter!

00:16:59.833 --> 00:17:01.542
Just a little more until
the 40% of my dreams!

00:17:01.542 --> 00:17:03.417
It's good that this city's people...

00:17:03.417 --> 00:17:06.375
And there is smoke coming
from all over that very city...

00:17:06.375 --> 00:17:07.750
It's disturbing,
but I won't let it bother me!

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:11.000
If it stays this placid after
ACROSS has conquered the city,

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:12.583
this city will be easy to rule!

00:17:12.583 --> 00:17:14.917
Now, let's earn more and
more change at our current pace!

00:17:14.917 --> 00:17:17.500
What about conquering the city?

00:17:21.125 --> 00:17:22.667
With the earning of additional income,

00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:25.000
the conquest plan
is progressing favorably.

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:27.083
That is brilliant, Senior.

00:17:27.083 --> 00:17:30.292
Now, Hatchan, go investigate the
vending machine over there please.

00:17:30.292 --> 00:17:31.458
I understand.

00:17:31.458 --> 00:17:34.083
Oh, there are some where
some idiot is using gum

00:17:34.083 --> 00:17:36.208
to intercept the change,
so be careful!

00:17:36.208 --> 00:17:38.042
Daiten Core!

00:17:38.042 --> 00:17:40.292
--Man, you're so cool, myself!

00:17:40.292 --> 00:17:41.917
--Stupid!
--Man, you're so cool, myself!

00:17:41.917 --> 00:17:45.458
Stupid, stupid!

00:17:45.458 --> 00:17:48.667
What did you say?!
What you damn devil-kids need is...

00:17:48.667 --> 00:17:49.500
Electric Sun!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:50.458
"Smack!"

00:17:50.458 --> 00:17:51.708
"Giga Paper Fan!"

00:17:51.708 --> 00:17:53.250
What an immature guy.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.375
In the end,
this guy's idea of justice is...

00:17:56.167 --> 00:17:58.875
A change thief. An easy mark.

00:17:58.875 --> 00:18:02.000
Turning my finger around and around...

00:18:02.000 --> 00:18:03.083
Hey, you!

00:18:03.083 --> 00:18:06.542
Stealing change left in a vending
machine is unmistakably a...

00:18:06.542 --> 00:18:08.167
But y-you're...

00:18:08.167 --> 00:18:09.792
Miss Ayasugi...

00:18:09.792 --> 00:18:11.333
"Watanabe's Wild Imagination Part 2"

00:18:11.875 --> 00:18:13.167
Why are you here?

00:18:13.167 --> 00:18:15.292
Who might you be?

00:18:15.292 --> 00:18:17.833
It's me. The Watanabe that lives
in the same apartment as you.

00:18:17.833 --> 00:18:22.292
What? But why are you
dressed so weird like that?

00:18:22.292 --> 00:18:25.292
Tha-That's because... Hear me out.

00:18:26.292 --> 00:18:27.917
I've hidden it from you all this time,

00:18:27.917 --> 00:18:29.250
but I'm actually a champion of justice,

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:33.000
Daiten Ism of the
Municipal Force Daitenzin!

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.750
<i>You </i>are Daiten Ism?

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.667
The one who saved me
from danger so many times?

00:18:38.667 --> 00:18:41.250
I never knew that
was you, Mr. Watanabe.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:43.417
You can be angry
with me. I'll understand.

00:18:43.417 --> 00:18:46.250
I am so happy, Mr. Watanabe.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:49.667
I... I have always...

00:18:49.667 --> 00:18:55.208
Miss Ayasugi, it's okay. I know.

00:18:55.208 --> 00:18:58.417
I know that something like
that will never happen in reality,

00:18:58.417 --> 00:18:59.750
but...

00:19:01.542 --> 00:19:04.000
By the way, what are you doing?

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:06.583
Well, I am looking for change, and...

00:19:06.583 --> 00:19:07.917
Did you lose your
purse or something?

00:19:07.917 --> 00:19:09.250
Oh, no...

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.000
Oh, geez.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:14.583
Here, take this home with you.

00:19:14.583 --> 00:19:16.500
Oh, hold it, no need to thank me.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:18.667
I may not look it, but I'm
still a champion of justice.

00:19:18.667 --> 00:19:21.958
All right, I really appreciate it. Goodbye.

00:19:21.958 --> 00:19:23.042
Sure!

00:19:23.042 --> 00:19:26.750
This is... This is the true
duty of a champion of justice.

00:19:26.750 --> 00:19:27.917
Oh-ho!

00:19:27.917 --> 00:19:29.458
I-Iwata!

00:19:29.458 --> 00:19:31.583
I saw it! I <i>so </i>saw!

00:19:31.583 --> 00:19:33.625
"I really appreciate it."

00:19:33.625 --> 00:19:36.083
"This is the true duty
of a champion of justice."

00:19:38.292 --> 00:19:39.958
Mad, mad, mad!

00:19:39.958 --> 00:19:42.250
That's what you get for trying to
get in the way of the city's peace

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:44.708
when you're supposed
to be local civil servants!

00:19:44.708 --> 00:19:46.292
So there!

00:19:46.292 --> 00:19:48.083
We are also local civil servants.

00:19:48.083 --> 00:19:49.417
What, we are?

00:19:49.417 --> 00:19:53.292
We're going to get out of
here before the situation worsens.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.333
What? It came off of you, Sister.

00:19:59.333 --> 00:20:00.875
Lucky!

00:20:00.875 --> 00:20:02.542
Oh, me too.

00:20:02.542 --> 00:20:04.875
It seems that it
comes off automatically.

00:20:04.875 --> 00:20:06.208
In any case, let's go home.

00:20:06.208 --> 00:20:07.208
Okay!

00:20:07.208 --> 00:20:08.708
What about Senior Iwata and the others?

00:20:08.708 --> 00:20:11.208
Taking care of the
aftermath is the leader's job.

00:20:12.333 --> 00:20:15.417
Haha! Municipal Force
romantic comedy boy!

00:20:15.417 --> 00:20:17.583
Don't say another word! Don't talk!

00:20:17.583 --> 00:20:19.042
L-O-V-E!

00:20:19.042 --> 00:20:22.250
Take this! Megatron Bazooka!

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.667
You idiot!

00:20:28.083 --> 00:20:30.000
I-It didn't work!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.000
"It worked..."

00:20:31.667 --> 00:20:34.083
Take this, Rubble Machinegun!

00:20:34.083 --> 00:20:35.333
Rubble Shield!

00:20:35.333 --> 00:20:37.875
"...fools..."

00:20:38.333 --> 00:20:41.208
Mr. Kabapu, what
is the meaning of this?!

00:20:41.208 --> 00:20:43.000
After you dispatched the Daitenzin,

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.750
calls to the police and fire
departments are ceaseless!

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:47.792
The cabinet has
decided to mobilize the JSDF!

00:20:47.792 --> 00:20:50.750
Not only that, the Multinational
Coalition has already mobilized!

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.208
All of this is your responsibility!

00:20:52.208 --> 00:20:53.583
You better be prepared!

00:20:53.583 --> 00:20:56.708
Mr. Kabapu, are you listening to me?!

00:20:56.708 --> 00:20:58.708
Hey! Answer me, Kaba!

00:21:02.292 --> 00:21:03.625
Watanabe!

00:21:03.625 --> 00:21:05.125
Iwata!

00:21:09.375 --> 00:21:11.583
There it is! The Triple Cross-Counter!

00:21:11.583 --> 00:21:13.250
Just a little.

00:21:16.583 --> 00:21:18.333
"Double Giga Paper Fans!"

00:21:20.167 --> 00:21:21.750
"That's ten..."

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:22.417
"Hm?"

00:21:24.583 --> 00:21:25.667
Ready to drop.

00:21:25.667 --> 00:21:26.708
Ready to drop.

00:21:26.708 --> 00:21:28.208
Dropping!

00:21:30.833 --> 00:21:32.500
"...this is bad..."

00:21:36.333 --> 00:21:40.750
So he donated 20,000
yen to ACROSS? Sweet!

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:44.292
We must be grateful to that
passing-by champion of justice.

00:21:44.292 --> 00:21:47.542
Here, Menchi,
eat plenty and grow big and fat.

00:21:50.583 --> 00:21:52.917
Thank you for the foo...

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:09.750
Jackal here. Mission accomplished.

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:11.542
Returning to base. Over.

00:22:11.542 --> 00:22:14.083
"F City"

00:22:17.625 --> 00:22:22.333
"Episode 18: Municipal Force Daitenzin"

00:22:22.333 --> 00:22:24.167
"Episode 18: Municipal Force Daitenzin"
"Today's Experiment..."

00:22:24.167 --> 00:22:25.958
"Episode 18: Municipal Force Daitenzin"
"Today's Experiment... Failed"

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:28.750
Still can't take it off!

00:22:50.917 --> 00:22:59.333
<i>I knew, ever since that day</i>

00:22:59.333 --> 00:23:06.750
<i>The reason you had approached me</i>

00:23:06.750 --> 00:23:14.833
<i>Tender and soft</i>

00:23:14.833 --> 00:23:23.625
<i>That my body is to your taste</i>

00:23:24.583 --> 00:23:32.375
<i>To your hunger-stricken eyes</i>

00:23:32.375 --> 00:23:40.250
<i>How does my body seem</i>

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:48.125
<i>If you are to eat me, do it in one blow</i>

00:23:48.125 --> 00:23:56.875
<i>So that the meat does not get hard</i>

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:05.208
I wanna run away!

00:24:05.208 --> 00:24:06.333
I don't wanna get eaten!

00:24:06.333 --> 00:24:07.458
I hate this show already!

00:24:07.458 --> 00:24:08.750
All that matters
in this world is money!

00:24:08.750 --> 00:24:09.917
I meet up with a mystery girl

00:24:09.917 --> 00:24:11.667
and travel all over
the world for some reason!

00:24:11.667 --> 00:24:12.917
Running, running,
and running away again!

00:24:12.917 --> 00:24:15.250
You'll have to wait
to see the punch line!

00:24:16.083 --> 00:24:17.833
Next time, Quack Experimental Anime,
Excel Saga,

00:24:17.833 --> 00:24:20.458
"Menchi's Great Adventure 2,
Around the World in 80 Hours!"

00:24:20.458 --> 00:24:21.583
Wow, this has actually been a preview.

00:24:21.583 --> 00:24:23.208
Or rather, what about
the scenes with us in them?

00:24:23.208 --> 00:24:28.594
I don't understand dog-ese.
